column9:
The copper tongue cleaner has been used for thousands of years for daily oral hygiene as it is one of the most sacred rituals of Ayurveda and is suggested to be performed every day as a part of Dinacharya.

Tongue cleaner very gently scrapes out unwanted toxins known as Aama. It removes accumulated bacteria from the tongue and supports the treatment of throat diseases.

&nbsp;

column150:
Inspect the coating on your tongue. Extend the tongue forward and hold the tongue cleaner backward towards the end of the tongue and gently scrape the toxins off of the tongue in the forward direction. Best performed early in the morning before meals.

&nbsp;
